    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_2b5cbd2a9693f146a8f27431a1eab9b19d65885fae43c50b929f87582517fe2b",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The hybrid factorization makes X a movable interface and the moment calculations make that movement quantitatively testable: enlarging X lengthens the prime factor while narrowing the effective zero window, the prime moment contributes (e^gamma log X)^{k^2}, and the modeled zero moment contributes the reciprocal cutoff scale, so their product can recover a cutoff-independent zeta moment.",
