    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b8954f1d8561a6cc418bfa039a4f73cdbc3fdb51acefc0835f6761d6d8b7f3fb",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Inverse-prime mollification converts the low-moment splitting test into finite twisted moments whose diagonal and off-diagonal burdens can be separated. For k=1 the twisted second moment and multiplicativity directly yield the reciprocal Mertens factor; for k=2 a specialized twisted fourth-moment formula exposes a diagonal Euler product with the predicted main constant and two structured off-diagonal sums, whose smallness depends on harmonic-sum estimates and cube-free local exclusions rather than on diagonal evaluation alone.",
