    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_cd814587d3e9c39f36b33c6ae96f92268f0d6d5cf5f6456ec8e144ac01a06775",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The zero factor reaches a characteristic-polynomial moment through a sequence of representation changes: cosine-integral smoothing localizes the zero statistic, periodicization turns it into a unit-circle symbol, density rescaling selects effective dimension N/(e^gamma log X), and Fisher-Hartwig analysis separates the symbol's local singularity from its smooth cutoff-dependent remainder to produce the Barnes-G constant and effective-dimension power.",
